{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1456998-getting-that-evangelion-like-feeling","id":1456998,"title":"Getting that Evangelion-like feeling...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-16T20:31:53-07:00","id":1456998,"title":"Getting that Evangelion-like feeling...","content":"Hi everybody! After watching Shin Evangelion 3.0+1.0, I was wondering as a alternative timeline to Aberrant, how would you build an Eva-like Aeon setting? I have some loose thoughts on how, but I'd love input.<br /> <br /> 1. The Hammersmith Experiment devastates the Earth in a catastrophe. Billions die. It's enough to trigger a brief nuclear exchange. Capital cities and top ten world cities are destroyed, adding to the already high death count.<br /> &gt; In this timeline the Hammersmith Experiment was deliberate. It was planned for, the damages known of, and considered acceptable collateral damage.<br /> &gt; Something important to the meta/narrative happened here. In Eva it was Adam, the (Arc)Angel of Destruction briefly waking up before being sealed into an embryonic state. Could we substate a high-quantum Aberrant for Adam here? Did Divis Mal try to make contact with a Q9/Q10 Aberrant trying to break the barrier that prevents Novas?<br /> <br /> 2. Giant, on the scale of 80-100ft. tall, Robots fighting Strange and Uncanny Alien Invaders. Whose invasion was planned for, but earlier than expected. Fortunately, the Test-type model(s) for the most part work, and the Prototype model(s) works well enough to be deemed worthy of upgrade. The Production Types are being rapidly finished (they were already 90% done) and being shipped to strategic sites.<br /> &gt; Who can pilot these robots are a very small group. It may not come down to the Chosen Children, but everyone is in need for more. It's not quite one-in-a-billion odds, but certainly less than 1\u2030 humanity can pilot. There are ongoing search efforts to locate new pilots, and research efforts to understand the phenomenon. <br /> &gt; Are Pilots Novas? Are they Psiads? Or does one need to be a Talent to Pilot the VARGs? Does one just need a particular narrative-mechanical Edge to pilot? I had ideas that the failed Hammersmith Experiment<br /> <br /> a) altered Talents so that there are Natural Talents, powered by Inspiration; Fool Talents, powered and haunted by desperation; and Jinx Talents, powered and defined by nihilism. Misato is a great example of a Natural Talent - She comes up with off-the-wall plans to defeat the Angels in ways no by-the-book General could. Shini is a Fool Talent, Shinji seems to have great luck, but always comes to rue his luck. Shinji's luck solve his immediate needs but not his emotional wants. Gendo, or possibly, Lorenz Keel, are Jinx Talents. They miraculously seem to make things worse off... yet their plans always, improbably succeed. Yet their plans involve nothing good to their fellow man.<br /> <br /> b) Created some kind of Spin to quantum phenomenon. This is important because differing quantum spins, or handiness, are mutually incompatible. You could even divide Quantum Powers and Mega Attributes into different left-handed and right-handedness. (Maybe corruption affects various chirality differently? It doesn't matter really, out alternate timeline ends with a Near-Third-Impact-like event so that we can sync back up to Aeon.) Our pilots may even an until now seen chirality, yawing in some w-dimension others can't access. Maybe the VARGs require that w-dimension to power their weapons/abilities. Maybe pilots can pick up those abilities, at a price of a little corruption. (Example Rei, Karow. They were more than human, but use of their abilities had short, and possibly long-term impacts to their health, sanity and humanity.<br /> <br /> That's all that I have right now. Love to hear what your thoughts are!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T20:49:35-07:00","id":1457000,"title":"","content":"Just a nitpick: the Hammersmith event could not have triggered a nuclear exchange. Nuclear weapons still don't exist at the time of the TC:Adventure! setting, let alone close to two decades earlier when the Hammersmith Event took place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T21:05:08-07:00","id":1457002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1456998-getting-that-evangelion-like-feeling?p=1457000#post1457000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a nitpick: the Hammersmith event could not have triggered a nuclear exchange. Nuclear weapons still don't exist at the time of the TC:Adventure! setting, let alone close to two decades earlier when the Hammersmith Event took place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oops. I thought that was the Space Station exploding. I guess I confused the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T21:18:39-07:00","id":1457003,"title":"","content":"Second Impact happened in Antarctica on September 13, 2000. Didn't the one Adventure! faction have a hidden Antarctic base where they locked up weird science stuff to keep it hidden from the world? Maybe something destabilized? Or maybe Divis Mal got impatient and tried activating his machine 18 years early, to disastrous results. Perhaps the Angels were sent by the Doyen to destroy humanity because of our quantum potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T04:23:30-07:00","id":1457018,"title":"","content":"I would go for N-Day created/awake/turn people into quantum powered giants.<br /> <br /> Evas are biotech and hardtech mixed, created using alien dna (from Lilith, a psionic being that is basically dead) and inspired super tech, that need to be piloted by talents.<br /> <br /> While I like the different talents idea I would keep it only as flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-17-2021, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}